  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043932",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-15805",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e44305e5-b7e3-5ae2-925c-9329f37823b8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Circle with a Line",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043932/assets/de12c0b5be8318cc21c62615d24125998c22d55d37abafdee37c103c3840cb71.png)\n\nFind the points where the circle ${x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=20$ intersects the line $x-3y=2$ (sketched above).",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation $x-3y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nTo find $x$-coordinates of the intersection points, we need to substitute $y=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+4)}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{10}{3})}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{20x}{9}+\\frac{100}{9} & =20 \\\\ \\frac{10{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{20x}{9}+\\frac{100}{9} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+10 & =18 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $y$-coordinates of the intersection points, we need to substitute $x=-4,2$ into the equation of the line and compute $y$-values. Start with $x=-4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first intersection point is $(-4,-2).$ Next, we plug in $x=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second intersection point is $(2,0).$\n\nTherefore, the line $x-3y=2$ intersects the circle ${x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=20$ at the points $(-4,-2)$ and $(2,0).$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$(-4,-2)$ and $(1,0)$",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
