  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043932",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-54242",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0d0e48e3-39ca-551a-80a4-dc7ff7855197",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying When a Circle Does Not Intersect with a Line",
      "problem": "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points where the circle $(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ intersects the line $y=-x+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $x$-coordinates of the intersection points, we need to substitute $y=-x+3$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(-x+3)^{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+1+{x}^{2}-6x+9 & =5 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x+5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we compute the discriminant $D$ of the above quadratic equation, then we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-4)^{2}-4\\cdot 2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =16-40 \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D=-24<0$, there are no real solutions to the equation $2{x}^{2}-4x+5=0.$\n\nHence, we conclude that the circle $(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ does not intersect the line $y=-x+3$ at any point.\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043932/assets/85c9bea054f2e246d62864b022e53a6f1d23886b0f0c9f8c80c8e0a5b1be9cd8.png)",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$-1$ and $4$",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$-1$ only",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$1$ and $3$",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$-3$ and $-1$",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The circle and the line do not intersect",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
